# A split card's mana value on the stack is that of the half cast (CR 202.3d, 709.3b), not the whole card's. Leave // Chance
# has mana value 6 in the hand, but Leave cast from it is a spell of mana value 2: Ashling, Rimebound's {W}{W} for "spells with
# mana value 4 or greater" may not pay for it (CR 106.6), so the Mox Pearl and Mox Jet mana does and the {W}{W} stays in the
# pool. Chance, cast by aftermath from the graveyard (CR 702.127a), is a spell of mana value 4: the {W}{W} pays two of its
# {3}{R} with the Mountain and Mox Ruby's {R}{R}. Leave returns the tapped Mox Sapphire to its owner's hand.

